course: dictionary
lesson: 4274
title: Great: one word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: The word great has more than one meaning, and the sentence tells you which one to use. Look at the words around it. In «a large-scale map shows a small area in great detail», the word detail is the clue. Great means a lot of detail, so it is about amount.
explain: Great can also mean very good, or important and famous. «The Head Chief says Taffy has made a great invention» means an important, clever idea, not a big one. In «Toad, the greatest boaster on the river bank», greatest means the most, the top of all the boasters.
explain: Great is also used in family words and in maths. Great-grandfather is your grandfather's father, one generation further back. In maths, «greater than» means bigger, and is written as >.
fact: Great means very good or excellent, as in a great idea.
fact: Great means very large in size or amount, as in a great big dog or a great deal.
fact: Great can mean important or famous, as in a great writer.
fact: In family words, great-grandma is your grandma's mother.
fact: Greater than means bigger, and is written as >: 7 > 4.
exercise: «The Head Chief says Taffy has made a great invention.» What does great mean here? | Very large in size | Very tired | Very wet | *Very good and important
exercise: What sign means «greater than»? | + | *> | < | =
exercise: In family words, what is your great-grandma? | Your mum's sister | *Your grandma's mother | Your aunt's daughter
test: «Dried tardigrades survive great cold, high pressure and radiation.» What does great mean here? | Very short | *Very large in amount or strength | Very kind
test: «Toad, the greatest boaster on the river bank.» What does greatest mean? | Smallest | *The most, the top of all | Quietest
exam: Which meaning of great fits «a great writer»? | Very wet | A great-grandparent | Very large in size | *Important or famous
